{%- comment -%}
  The product cards for one collection, as bare `<li>`s.

  This is rendered from two places and has to produce the same markup from
  both: the All Collections section draws it for the tab that is open when the
  page is built, and the `all-collections-grid` section draws it again for
  whichever collection the visitor asks for after that.

  That second caller is the reason the card's appearance is fixed here rather
  than passed in. The Section Rendering API resolves `?section_id=` against a
  section *file*, so a section fetched for a collection it was never placed on
  is rendered with its schema defaults and no template settings at all. Any
  card setting offered in the editor would therefore apply to the first tab
  and silently revert on every tab after it. One set of values, written once,
  is the only arrangement that cannot drift.

  What is safe to configure lives on the `<ul>` instead — the column counts —
  because that element belongs to the section and is never swapped out.

  Only the list items are produced here. The list itself is the section's.

  Accepts:
  - grid_collection: {Object} the collection to draw
  - section_id: {String} the id of the section the cards are being drawn into

  Usage:
  {% render 'all-collections-grid', grid_collection: collection, section_id: section.id %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Without a `paginate` tag Shopify hands over the first 50 products of a
    collection and stops. That is the ceiling here, and it is why the link out
    to the collection's own page appears when a collection has more — a
    paginated grid cannot survive being swapped in by fetch without carrying
    its page links along with it, and a link to the real collection page is
    the honest answer rather than a half-built one.
  endcomment
  assign shown = grid_collection.products.size
  assign total = grid_collection.all_products_count
-%}

{%- if shown == 0 -%}
  <li class="acl__span acl__empty">
    {{ 'sections.collection_template.empty' | t }}
  </li>
{%- else -%}
  {%- for product in grid_collection.products -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign lazy_load = true
      if forloop.index <= 3
        assign lazy_load = false
      endif
    -%}
    <li class="grid__item">
      {% render 'card-product',
        card_product: product,
        media_aspect_ratio: 'square',
        show_secondary_image: false,
        show_vendor: false,
        show_rating: true,
        quick_add: 'standard',
        lazy_load: lazy_load,
        skip_styles: true,
        section_id: section_id,
        product_view_context: 'collection'
      %}
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if total > shown -%}
    <li class="acl__span acl__more">
      <a class="acl__more-link" href="{{ grid_collection.url }}">
        {{- grid_collection.title }} &mdash; all {{ total }} products
        <svg class="acl__more-arrow" viewBox="0 0 34 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path
            d="M0 5h31.5M27.5 1 32 5l-4.5 4"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.4"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </li>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
